<refentry xmlns="http://docbook.org/ns/docbook" version="5.2" id="process_spikegrouper">

	<refmeta>
		<refentrytitle>process_spikegrouper</refentrytitle>
		<manvolnum>1</manvolnum>
	</refmeta>

	<refnamediv>
		<refname>process_spikegrouper</refname>
		<refpurpose>discover optimal spike detection channel groups from a high-pass filtered signal.</refpurpose>
	</refnamediv>

	<refsynopsisdiv>
		<cmdsynopsis>
		<command>process_spikegrouper</command>
		<arg choice="plain"><option>--fil</option> <replaceable>file</replaceable></arg>
		<arg choice="plain"><option>--yaml</option> <replaceable>file</replaceable></arg>
		<arg choice="plain"><option>--nchannels</option> <replaceable>N</replaceable></arg>
		<arg choice="plain"><option>--sampling-rate</option> <replaceable>SR</replaceable></arg>
		<arg><option>--nbits</option> <replaceable>N</replaceable></arg>
		<arg><option>--threshold-factor</option> <replaceable>F</replaceable></arg>
		<arg><option>--refractory-ms</option> <replaceable>R</replaceable></arg>
		<arg><option>--coincidence-ms</option> <replaceable>W</replaceable></arg>
		<arg><option>--window-sec</option> <replaceable>T</replaceable></arg>
		<arg><option>--max-sub-groups</option> <replaceable>K</replaceable></arg>
		<arg><option>--min-channels</option> <replaceable>M</replaceable></arg>
		<arg><option>--max-merged-size</option> <replaceable>S</replaceable></arg>
		<arg><option>--channel-overlap</option> <replaceable>N</replaceable></arg>
		<arg><option>--exclude-channels</option> <replaceable>LIST</replaceable></arg>
		<arg><option>--nsamples</option> <replaceable>S</replaceable></arg>
		<arg><option>--peak-sample</option> <replaceable>P</replaceable></arg>
		<arg><option>--nfeatures</option> <replaceable>F</replaceable></arg>
		<arg><option>--cpu</option></arg>
		<arg><option>-v</option></arg>
		</cmdsynopsis>
	</refsynopsisdiv>

	<refsect1>
		<title>Description</title>
		<para>
			<command>process_spikegrouper</command> analyses a high-pass filtered
			<replaceable>.fil</replaceable> file to discover optimal spike detection
			channel sub-groups and rewrites the
			<literal>spikeDetection.channelGroups</literal> section of the session
			YAML parameter file with the result.
		</para>
		<para>
			It is called by the <command>ndm_spikegrouper</command> pipeline script
			and operates only on YAML parameter files.  Convert XML sessions to YAML
			first with <command>ndm_xml2yaml</command>.
		</para>
		<para>
			Grouping is bounded by the <literal>anatomicalDescription.channelGroups</literal>
			entries in the YAML file: channels from different anatomical groups (shanks)
			are never merged.  Within each anatomical group the algorithm computes a
			spike-coincidence similarity matrix and clusters channels by Ward
			agglomerative clustering, choosing the number of sub-groups that maximises
			the average silhouette score.  A post-clustering merge pass re-combines
			adjacent sub-groups that have high inter-boundary coincidence.
		</para>
	</refsect1>

	<refsect1>
		<title>Required Options</title>
		<variablelist>
			<varlistentry>
				<term><option>--fil</option> <replaceable>file</replaceable></term>
				<listitem>
					<para>
						Path to the high-pass filtered binary signal file
						(<replaceable>.fil</replaceable>).  Must be raw int16,
						channel-interleaved, no header.
					</para>
				</listitem>
			</varlistentry>
			<varlistentry>
				<term><option>--yaml</option> <replaceable>file</replaceable></term>
				<listitem>
					<para>
						Path to the YAML session parameter file.  The
						<literal>spikeDetection.channelGroups</literal> section will be
						atomically replaced with the discovered groups; all other content
						is preserved verbatim.
					</para>
				</listitem>
			</varlistentry>
			<varlistentry>
				<term><option>--nchannels</option> <replaceable>N</replaceable></term>
				<listitem>
					<para>Total number of channels in the <replaceable>.fil</replaceable> file.</para>
				</listitem>
			</varlistentry>
			<varlistentry>
				<term><option>--sampling-rate</option> <replaceable>SR</replaceable></term>
				<listitem>
					<para>
						Acquisition sampling rate in Hz.  Used to convert millisecond
						timing parameters to sample counts.
					</para>
				</listitem>
			</varlistentry>
		</variablelist>
	</refsect1>

	<refsect1>
		<title>Detection Options</title>
		<variablelist>
			<varlistentry>
				<term><option>--nbits</option> <replaceable>N</replaceable></term>
				<listitem><para>Bits per sample in the <replaceable>.fil</replaceable> file.  Default: 16.</para></listitem>
			</varlistentry>
			<varlistentry>
				<term><option>--threshold-factor</option> <replaceable>F</replaceable></term>
				<listitem>
					<para>
						Threshold multiplier: threshold = <replaceable>F</replaceable> ×
						median(|signal|) / 0.6745.  Identical to the estimator used by
						<command>process_medianthreshold</command>, so thresholds are
						consistent with what <command>ndm_extractspikes</command> will
						use.  Default: 3.0.
					</para>
				</listitem>
			</varlistentry>
			<varlistentry>
				<term><option>--refractory-ms</option> <replaceable>R</replaceable></term>
				<listitem><para>Minimum inter-event interval in milliseconds for threshold-crossing detection.  Default: 1.0.</para></listitem>
			</varlistentry>
			<varlistentry>
				<term><option>--coincidence-ms</option> <replaceable>W</replaceable></term>
				<listitem>
					<para>
						Half-window for spike coincidence: events on two channels are
						considered coincident if they fall within ±<replaceable>W</replaceable> ms
						of each other.  Default: 0.4.
					</para>
				</listitem>
			</varlistentry>
			<varlistentry>
				<term><option>--window-sec</option> <replaceable>T</replaceable></term>
				<listitem><para>Seconds of the <replaceable>.fil</replaceable> file to analyse.  Default: 60.</para></listitem>
			</varlistentry>
		</variablelist>
	</refsect1>

	<refsect1>
		<title>Grouping Options</title>
		<variablelist>
			<varlistentry>
				<term><option>--max-sub-groups</option> <replaceable>K</replaceable></term>
				<listitem><para>Maximum number of sub-groups to create per anatomical group.  Default: 6.</para></listitem>
			</varlistentry>
			<varlistentry>
				<term><option>--min-channels</option> <replaceable>M</replaceable></term>
				<listitem><para>Minimum channels required in any sub-group.  Groups smaller than this are absorbed into their nearest neighbour.  Default: 4.</para></listitem>
			</varlistentry>
			<varlistentry>
				<term><option>--max-merged-size</option> <replaceable>S</replaceable></term>
				<listitem>
					<para>
						Maximum number of channels in any final group after the
						post-clustering merge pass.  Default: 12.
					</para>
				</listitem>
			</varlistentry>
			<varlistentry>
				<term><option>--channel-overlap</option> <replaceable>N</replaceable></term>
				<listitem>
					<para>
						Number of channels to borrow from each neighbouring group and
						append to this group's channel list.  Borrowed channels provide
						spatial context without changing core group boundaries.
						Default: 0 (disabled).
					</para>
				</listitem>
			</varlistentry>
			<varlistentry>
				<term><option>--exclude-channels</option> <replaceable>LIST</replaceable></term>
				<listitem>
					<para>
						Comma-separated list of channel indices to exclude from all
						groups, e.g. <literal>3,7,42</literal>.  Useful for known bad or
						reference channels.
					</para>
				</listitem>
			</varlistentry>
		</variablelist>
	</refsect1>

	<refsect1>
		<title>Output Group Metadata</title>
		<variablelist>
			<varlistentry>
				<term><option>--nsamples</option> <replaceable>S</replaceable></term>
				<listitem><para>Value to write for <literal>nSamples</literal> in newly created groups.  If not specified, the value is inherited from the matching existing spike group.  Default: 52.</para></listitem>
			</varlistentry>
			<varlistentry>
				<term><option>--peak-sample</option> <replaceable>P</replaceable></term>
				<listitem><para>Value to write for <literal>peakSampleIndex</literal> in newly created groups.  Default: 26.</para></listitem>
			</varlistentry>
			<varlistentry>
				<term><option>--nfeatures</option> <replaceable>F</replaceable></term>
				<listitem><para>Value to write for <literal>nFeatures</literal> in newly created groups.  Default: 3.</para></listitem>
			</varlistentry>
		</variablelist>
	</refsect1>

	<refsect1>
		<title>Other Options</title>
		<variablelist>
			<varlistentry>
				<term><option>--cpu</option></term>
				<listitem>
					<para>
						Force the CPU code path even when a CUDA device is available.
						Available only in CUDA builds.
					</para>
				</listitem>
			</varlistentry>
			<varlistentry>
				<term><option>-v</option></term>
				<listitem><para>Verbose output: per-channel thresholds and event counts, silhouette scores, merge decisions, and final group assignments.</para></listitem>
			</varlistentry>
		</variablelist>
	</refsect1>

	<refsect1>
		<title>Algorithm</title>
		<para>
			For each anatomical group, the algorithm:
		</para>
		<orderedlist>
			<listitem>
				<para>Loads up to <option>--window-sec</option> seconds of the <replaceable>.fil</replaceable> file.</para>
			</listitem>
			<listitem>
				<para>Estimates per-channel noise as
					threshold = <option>--threshold-factor</option> ×
					median(|signal|) / 0.6745.</para>
			</listitem>
			<listitem>
				<para>Detects threshold crossings with the specified refractory period.</para>
			</listitem>
			<listitem>
				<para>Builds an N×N spike-coincidence similarity matrix C where
					C[i,j] = coincident events(i,j) / (events(i) + 1),
					then symmetrises as (C + C^T) / 2.</para>
			</listitem>
			<listitem>
				<para>Applies Ward agglomerative clustering on the distance matrix (1 − C),
					selecting the number of clusters in [1, <option>--max-sub-groups</option>]
					that maximises the average silhouette score subject to the
					<option>--min-channels</option> constraint.</para>
			</listitem>
			<listitem>
				<para>Runs a greedy merge pass on adjacent sub-groups: repeatedly merges
					the adjacent pair with the highest inter-group coincidence while
					respecting <option>--max-merged-size</option>.</para>
			</listitem>
			<listitem>
				<para>Optionally extends each group by borrowing
					<option>--channel-overlap</option> channels from its neighbours.</para>
			</listitem>
			<listitem>
				<para>Atomically rewrites the YAML file's
					<literal>spikeDetection.channelGroups</literal> section.</para>
			</listitem>
		</orderedlist>
		<para>
			The computationally intensive threshold estimation and coincidence matrix
			construction are accelerated by CUDA when built with <literal>USE_CUDA</literal>
			and a device is available.  When CUDA is absent, OpenMP parallelises the
			per-channel threshold/detection loop and the O(N²) coincidence matrix
			construction.
		</para>
	</refsect1>

	<refsect1>
		<title>Exit Status</title>
		<variablelist>
			<varlistentry>
				<term>0</term>
				<listitem><para>Success.</para></listitem>
			</varlistentry>
			<varlistentry>
				<term>1</term>
				<listitem><para>Error: missing required argument, YAML parse failure, or I/O error.</para></listitem>
			</varlistentry>
			<varlistentry>
				<term>11</term>
				<listitem><para>Input missing: the <replaceable>.fil</replaceable> or YAML file could not be opened, or the <replaceable>.fil</replaceable> file is too small.</para></listitem>
			</varlistentry>
		</variablelist>
	</refsect1>

	<refsect1>
		<title>See Also</title>
		<para>
			<citerefentry><refentrytitle>process_extractspikes</refentrytitle><manvolnum>1</manvolnum></citerefentry>,
			<citerefentry><refentrytitle>process_medianfilter</refentrytitle><manvolnum>1</manvolnum></citerefentry>,
			<citerefentry><refentrytitle>process_medianthreshold</refentrytitle><manvolnum>1</manvolnum></citerefentry>
		</para>
	</refsect1>

</refentry>
